      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T08:49:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hopefully clients of the memory store never see this (there really isn\u0027t much you can do with an interrupt except for retrying, which a good public API should do automatically if this is a concern). Therefore this should be purely internal to the memory store.\n\nI think the simplest way of not exposing this is to not create it, and return ERROR_GENERIC instead in the interrupted maintenance case.\n\nA maybe better way of handling this is to have a flag for internal messages. You could define a space for internal messages like this :\n\n  ...\n  public static final int ERROR_STORAGE \u003d -4;\n  // Error codes below are internal.\n  static final int ERROR_INTERNAL_BASE \u003d -1_000_000_000;\n  static final int ERROR_INTERNAL_INTERRUPTED \u003d ERROR_INTERNAL_BASE - 1;\n  static final int ERROR_INTERNAL_NOT_ENOUGH_RECORDS \u003d ERROR_INTERNAL_BASE - 2;",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "c30ced3affcad829da09ddf204797842c13b7399",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
